## Step 5: Cross-service synthesis write-back

Read the `file-research` skill first:
`/Users/charsmith/Documents/the_vault/dp-knowledge-base/.claude/skills/file-research/SKILL.md`

It is the authoritative protocol. Summary:

**5a — Create the research doc**

Create `research/<topic>/<topic>.md` with this frontmatter:
```yaml
---
question: <the specific question the research answered, ≤20 words>
date: <YYYY-MM-DD>
audience: "internal (Charles)"
sources:
  docs:
    - url: <Manuals or Google Docs URL>
      title: "<title>"
  tools:
    - tools/<service>/overview.md   # every tools/ file materially used
repos: [<repo-name>, ...]
---
```

The body of the file is the coordinator's synthesized output — the full report with all evidence citations preserved. Every code citation must include: file path, line number, AND `https://github.netflix.net/<org>/<repo>/blob/<branch>/<file>#L<line>`. Every doc citation must include the full URL.

**5b — Update research.md index**

Add a row to the table in `research.md` (newest first):
```
| <YYYY-MM-DD> | <question ≤12 words> | [[research/<topic>/<topic>]] | <source types> |
```

**5c — Add bidirectional backlinks**

For every `tools/<service>/overview.md` the research materially used, append or add to its `## See Also` section:
```markdown
## See Also

- [[research/<topic>/<topic>]] — <one-line summary of what the research covers> (<Month YYYY>)
```

**5d — Commit**

```bash
cd /Users/charsmith/Documents/the_vault/dp-knowledge-base
git add research/<topic>/
git add research.md
git add tools/<touched-service>/   # for each backlink added
git commit -m "research: <topic>"
```

